{title: Into the Deep}
{artist: Citipointe Music, Chardon Lewis}
{key: G#m}
{tempo: 74}

{comment: Verse}
When my [G#m]hands stretch [B]out towards the [E]sky
You [G#m]never [B]let me [E]run dry
When I [G#m]dive into [B]the depths of [E]You
My heart is made [G#m]anew, [B]Jesus in [E]You

[F#](Into chorus)

{comment: Chorus}
Your [B]love is a flood and I’m [F#]caught in the current
Of Your [E]living waters, It’s Your [G#m]love, It’s Your [F#]love
Your [G#m]presence is a flood and I’m [F#/D#]caught in the wonder
You have [E]taken me over, You have [G#m]won my [F#]heart

{comment: Bridge}
[G#m]  Into the [F#/D#]deep I will go with You
[E]  Submerge my [F#]feet to my head in all of You
[G#m]  As Your [F#/D#]presence falls, I am drowned in Your love
[E]  Immerse me, [F#]Immerse me
